WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.690
Everything up to here, we could do by hand, slowly.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.141
An agent with write access, running while we sleep, is exactly as useful

00:00:08.191 --> 00:00:11.948
and exactly as dangerous.

00:00:13.148 --> 00:00:20.066
So the rule is: keys, not prompts. Telling an agent not to do something is a preference, not a boundary.

00:00:20.616 --> 00:00:23.430
Then six roles, four of them read-only.

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:30.937
The ingestor. The linker. The reviewer. The researcher. The graph analyst.

00:00:30.987 --> 00:00:31.936
And the curator.

00:00:32.486 --> 00:00:42.188
Ingest, daily. Link, weekly. Lint, weekly. Review, weekly. Metrics, monthly.

00:00:42.288 --> 00:00:46.014
Each run leaves a log entry, a commit, and a report.

00:00:46.564 --> 00:00:49.256
Subagents get their own context.

00:00:49.306 --> 00:00:53.684
Fan out for research, independent sources, and verification.

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:55.738
Related sources go in sequence.

00:00:56.288 --> 00:01:02.221
Skills teach repeatable behaviour. Commands are shortcuts that point at a skill.

00:01:02.271 --> 00:01:04.214
The behaviour belongs in the skill.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:09.882
That's chapter six, agents. Start with page one: Guardrails.
